Business Rules:

BR-026: A seafarer can have at most one active assignment at any time. An active assignment is one where the actual sign-off date has not been recorded.
Rationale: A person cannot physically be on two vessels simultaneously. This is also a regulatory requirement for flag state records.

BR-027: The assignment rank may differ from the seafarer's current rank. Rationale: Operational flexibility — a Chief Officer might sail as Master on a
smaller vessel, or a Second Engineer might fill in as Chief Engineer. The assignment records what role they're actually performing.

BR-028: Only ACTIVE vessels can receive crew assignments. Rationale: You cannot staff a vessel that is out of service.

BR-029: Only ACTIVE seafarers can be assigned to vessels. Rationale: Inactive seafarers are not available for deployment.

BR-030: Sign-on date is mandatory. Rationale: Every assignment must have a clear start date for regulatory, payroll, and operational tracking.

BR-031: Sign-off date must be on or after the sign-on date. Rationale: A seafarer cannot leave a vessel before they boarded.

BR-032: Sign-off is a one-time action. Once an assignment is completed, it cannot be modified. Rationale: Completed assignments are historical records
used for regulatory reporting and payroll. Tampering breaks compliance.

BR-033: Signing off a seafarer does not change the seafarer's status. They remain ACTIVE and available for new assignments. Rationale: Completing a voyage
is normal operations, not a status change.

BR-034: The crew roster shows only active assignments (where actual sign-off date is null). Rationale: The roster answers "who is on board right now",
not "who has ever been on board."

BR-035: Only ACTIVE assignments can be cancelled. Completed assignments are historical records and must not be altered. Rationale:
Regulatory and payroll compliance.

BR-036: Cancellation is a soft status change, not a delete. The record persists for audit purposes. Rationale: Traceability — if an assignment
was created and then cancelled, that action trail should be visible.